{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]The shepherds in the field by night
Were [F]watching flocks of [C]sheep
When [Am7]glory shone with [G6]sudden [Cmaj7/G]light
[F]And woke [Cmaj7/G]them from their [G]sleep
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Fear [Am7]not, the shining [F]angel [C]said
[F]Great joy [G]to all I [Am]bring
In [Am7]Bethlehem a [G]manger [C]bed
Now [F]holds your [Cmaj7/G]Lord and [C]King
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
And then a host of angels came
And [F]filled the midnight [C]sky
They [Am7]sang the glory [G6]of his name
To [F]God be [Cmaj7/G]praise on [G]high
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
And [Am7]peace on earth to [F]all be[C]low
With [F]whom the [G6]Lord is [Am]pleased
So [Am7]let us all to [G6]Bethlehem [C]go
